# Preferences

Living **user project preferences** — follow them by default. Prefer matching the user’s style; if a preference conflicts with a hard constraint (security, correctness, Next.js/App Router requirements), prioritize the constraint and note the trade-off.

Current preferences:

- One TSX file, one exported component: a `.tsx` UI module has exactly one exported function that returns JSX. Do not export multiple components from the same file. Non-UI modules (`types.ts`, services, utils) are exempt; local non-exported helpers inside the file are allowed.
- Do not add re-export / barrel pass-through modules (`export … from "…"` that only forward another module). Import from the module that defines the symbol (e.g. `@/shared/services/types`, `@/back-end/common/errors`). Exception: UI kit barrels that re-export components defined in the same file (shadcn pattern) are fine.
- Treat `src/front-end/components/ui/*` (shadcn) as installed external third-party components. Do not modify, refactor, rename, or “clean up” them without the user’s explicit request or approval.
- Prefer array methods (`forEach`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, etc.) over `for...of` / classic `for` when iterating collections. Do not rewrite `forEach`/`map` into `for...of` for lint.
- Type-only imports must use `import type { ... }` (e.g. `import type { IData } from "@/shared/services/types"`).
- Component / feature props and related interfaces live in a co-located `types.ts` at the directory level (e.g. `src/front-end/components/budgets/types.ts`, `src/front-end/components/login/types.ts`, `src/app/login/types.ts`). Do not keep props interfaces inline in the component / page / layout file. Import with `import type { IBudgetsProps } from "@/front-end/components/budgets/types"`. Shared cross-cutting types stay in `@/shared/services/types` (or the module that owns them). App-route-only props (e.g. page `searchParams`) go in that route’s `types.ts` under `src/app/` — never inline in `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`.
- Enforce layer split: `src/front-end/` (UI), `src/shared/` (isomorphic), `src/back-end/` (server). Allowed: FE → shared + server-actions; BE → shared + lib; shared → neither FE nor BE; app → FE + server-actions. Forbidden: BE → FE, shared → FE/BE, FE → DAL/mappers/prisma.
- Logging: use `@/shared/services/logger.service` (`logError` / `logWarn` / `logInfo`) with the matching severity. Do not use bare `console.*` for app logs. Prefix every message with the logical area in brackets, e.g. `[auth] AUTH_EMAIL and AUTH_PASSWORD environment variables are not set`, `[pots] Failed to get pots data`.
